<Plain title="ytk privacy policy" description="What ytk does with Google account data.">
  <h1>ytk privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated 18 November 2026</p>

  <p>ytk is a private tool run by Khanh Nguyen on his own computer to manage his own YouTube channels and Google Drive. The only person who signs in to it is its owner.</p>

  <h2>What it accesses</h2>
  <p>When the owner signs in with Google, ytk may use these permissions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>YouTube</strong>: upload videos, set titles, descriptions, thumbnails and playlists, and read channel and video details;</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube Analytics</strong>: read view, watch-time and retention reports for the owner's channels;</li>
    <li><strong>Google Drive</strong>: create folders and upload video files to the owner's Drive.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the data goes</h2>
  <p>Sign-in tokens and any data read from Google are stored only on the owner's computer. ytk has no server. It does not sell, share or transfer Google user data to anyone, and does not use it for advertising or to train AI models.</p>
  <p>ytk's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Its use of YouTube API Services is subject to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Removing access</h2>
  <p>Access can be revoked at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Deleting the local token files removes everything ytk keeps.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:khanhng93@proton.me">khanhng93@proton.me</a></p>
</Plain>
